pan><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund I the Old was king of Poland and grand duke of Lithuania from 1506 to 1548.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-ii-augustus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-ii-augustus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismund II Augustus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund II Augustus was King of Poland and Grand Duke of Lithuania, the last of the Jagiellonian dynasty, who died in 1572.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-iii-vasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismund III Vasa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund III Vasa was king of Poland and grand duke of Lithuania from 1587 to 1632, and king of Sweden from 1592 until he was deposed in 1599.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-of-burgundy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismund of Burgundy</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund of Burgundy was king of the Burgundians from 516 to 524.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-archduke-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismund, Archduke of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund, Archduke of Austria, ruled Tyrol and Further Austria from 1446 to 1490.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismund, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund of Luxembourg was King of Hungary from 1387, King of the Romans from 1411, King of Bohemia from 1419 and Holy Roman Emperor from 1433.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siglo-xx-mine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siglo-xx-mine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siglo XX mine</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Siglo XX is a large tin mine at Llallagua in the department of Potosí, Bolivia, developed by Simón Patiño in the early twentieth century and nationalised in 1952.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigmaringen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigmaringen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigmaringen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigmaringen is a town on the upper Danube in Baden-Württemberg, Germany, dominated by a castle on a rock above the river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigmund-freud"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigmund-freud.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigmund Freud</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigmund Freud was an Austrian neurologist who founded psychoanalysis, working in Vienna from the late nineteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigmundur-brestisson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigmundur-brestisson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigmundur Brestisson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</